      {
        "id": 87391,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-23T22:54:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Braithwhite\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/braithwhite/48/1854_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Braithwhite:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>stuff</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>But there are sets of Five and Six and Eight and Ten as well, they just don't always show up in the same cultures.&nbsp; (For isntance, both China and Japan had five-element systems, while the Eightfold Path is central to Buddhism.)&nbsp; \"Catholicism\" as an answer will have to do, I guess.</p>",
