      {
        "id": 87399,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-25T09:18:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well I'm not a One True anything guy, and I loved the concept of different Rings gaining power from different mental states (calling it the Emotional Spectrum is questionable since Willpower isn't really an emotion, though you could label it Determination and it'd be closer).&nbsp; However, I strongly dislike the idea that the Red, Orange and Yellow rings are not only used exclusively by evil people, but even force you to be evil in order to use them - the Red ones make you a berserk killing machine, and you can't even make constructs with them.&nbsp; And there's only ever one Orange Lantern, which just stinks.</p><p>I have a headcanon/fanfic/Elseworlds thing where the other six Corps have existed since the beginning, all of them work more or less the same way except for the emotion involved, and all of them can be used by any number of people for good or for ill.&nbsp; Guy Gardner becomes a heroic Red Lantern, while Hal Jordan is the Green Lantern Corps's ambassador to the Yellow Corps, with Sinestro reciprocating; the two have an extremely uneasy alliance rather than actually fighting.&nbsp; John Stewart thusly becomes the \"standard\" Green Lantern of Earth, and Kyle Rayner was in some high-level advisory position involving either the Guardians or the Ion entity.&nbsp; It's been a while since I made all this up, so I'm unclear on some of the details.&nbsp; But I was immensely fond of some of the characters I started making up for it, including a heroic lady Orange Lantern who I really liked...her version of Greed was more like Luxury, she wanted everyone to wallow in obscene quantities of wealth, and basically used her Ring to grant wishes to everybody so they could all live like kings and queens.&nbsp; She would fight evil by bribing the villains into laying down their arms, and then the \"good\" Yellow Lanterns (including Batman) would get on her case for being an enabler instead of a punisher.</p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
