      {
        "id": 87400,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-26T10:36:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Greywind\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/greywind/48/2006_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Greywind:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Anything that resurrected Hal Jordan and ceased Rayner's run as the one true Green Lantern pretty much killed it for me.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The comic itself is written superbly and effectively embodies many tropes comics utilize.&nbsp; Resurrection and older characters reasserting themselves as the \"signature\" character of that superhero title are huge themes in this comic.&nbsp; Barry Allen and Hal Jordan reassert themselves in a world that has moved on.&nbsp; Many of their friends have been dead for years and the world is more jaded and dark than they remember.&nbsp; Older characters are reanimated as Black Lantern monstrocities that manipulate heroes and villains to further their agenda of ending all life.&nbsp; It's an examination of the nature of bringing DC characters back from the dead.</p>\n<p>Besides, Rayner is basically space Jesus as the one White Lantern in Green Lantern: New Guardians, and the Green Lantern Corps is essentially Exxon Valdez since it has recently been revealed that the various lantern corps drain the energy that powers the universe.<br><br>Basically, the current run is terrible.&nbsp; Kyle Rayner's current comic is terrible.&nbsp; It would still be terrible even if it were Hal, Guy, John, Simon, or Rot Lop \"F-Sharp Bell Corps\" Fan.&nbsp; It's bad writing.&nbsp; Not bad characters.<br><br>I'll take good writing with a less interesting character in a good comic rather than an interesting character being lame in a terrible comic.</p>",
        "post_number": 32,
        "post_type": 1,
